{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2020-09-28 18:30:00', 'title': "PG&E CORP SAYS COMPENSATION COMMITTEE APPROVED AMENDMENTS TO CO'S 2012 OFFICER SEVERANCE POLICY", 'text': 'PG&E CORP -  ON SEPTEMBER 24 COMPENSATION COMMITTEE APPROVED AMENDMENTS TO PG&E CORPORATION 2012 OFFICER SEVERANCE POLICY.PG&E CORP - CHRIS FOSTER TO GET A MONTHLY FEE OF $20,000 PER MONTH FOR HIS SERVICE AS INTERIM CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER.PG&E - BOARD CAN CANCEL, REQUIRE FORFEITURE OF CERTAIN PAYMENTS FROM CERTAIN EXECUTIVES IN CASE OF FELONY CONVICTION OF CO RELATED TO PUBLIC SAFETY.PG&E - CAN RECOUP/REQUIRE REIMBURSEMENT FROM SOME EXECUTIVES IF THEY ENGAGED IN MISCONDUCT, CONTRIBUTING TO ACTION/OMISSIONS ON WHICH CONVICTION IS BASED.'}{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2020-09-27 17:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E SAYS CONDUCTS PUBLIC SAFETY POWER SHUTOFFS IN RESPONSE TO HIGH-WIND EVENT, SCOPE OF EVENT REDUCED TO 65,000', 'text': 'PG&E CONDUCTS PUBLIC SAFETY POWER SHUTOFFS IN RESPONSE TO HIGH-WIND EVENT, SCOPE OF EVENT REDUCED TO 65,000.IN TOTAL POWER SHUTOFF EVENT IS EXPECTED TO IMPACT APPROXIMATELY 65,000 CUSTOMERS IN PORTIONS OF 16 COUNTIES.SOME CUSTOMERS MAY EXPERIENCE OUTAGES UNRELATED TO THIS PSPS EVENT DUE TO REQUESTS FROM CAL FIRE.PSPS EVENT WILL AFFECT CUSTOMERS IN PORTIONS OF 16 COUNTIES, PRIMARILY IN NORTHERN AND CENTRAL SIERRA REGION.TWO CUSTOMERS WITHIN SONOMA COUNTY AND 15 CUSTOMERS IN KERN COUNTY ARE ALSO EXPECTED TO BE INCLUDED IN SCOPE OF THIS PSPS.BASED ON WIND FORECASTS, DE-ENERGIZATION FOR SECOND WAVE OF 54,000 CUSTOMERS WILL BEGIN AT APPROXIMATELY 4:00 P.M. ON SUNDAY AFTERNOON.POWER IS EXPECTED TO BE OUT OVERNIGHT SUNDAY INTO MONDAY FOR ALL CUSTOMERS.'}{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2020-09-27 01:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E SAYS FOR PUBLIC SAFETY DUE TO SEVERE WEATHER, EXPECTS TO TURN OFF POWER TO ABOUT 89,000 CUSTOMERS IN PARTS OF 16 COUNTIES', 'text': 'FOR PUBLIC SAFETY DUE TO SEVERE WEATHER AND WIND, PG&E EXPECTS TO TURN OFF POWER TO APPROXIMATELY 89,000 CUSTOMERS IN PARTS OF 16 COUNTIES.'}